-- A BREACH BY a list written as the FIRST operand of a RAND, under a GIVETH.
-- The GIVETH's type reaches both operands, so the checker knows the party
-- type before it reads the list, and decides the reading by it: under a
-- party type that is itself the list's type the list is ONE party, and under
-- its element type the list names one party per element. Without a GIVETH
-- the same shapes are refused (not-ok/tc/breach-by-list-needs-party-type.l4).
-- (From unstable's 9d620c355; the first case is `the pair, breach first` in
-- unstable's ok/every/run-blame.l4. #817, which this branch is built on and
-- which has no blame list, accepts it too, as one party.)

DECLARE Step IS ONE OF deliver

-- The pair as one party: the BREACH names the list once.
GIVETH A DEONTIC (LIST OF STRING) Step
`the pair, breach first` MEANS
    (BREACH BY (LIST "a", "b") BECAUSE "declared against the pair")
    RAND
    (PARTY (LIST "a", "b") MUST deliver WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `the pair, breach first` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 20

-- Each member as a party: the BREACH names "a" and "b".
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING Step
`each of the pair, breach first` MEANS
    (BREACH BY (LIST "a", "b") BECAUSE "declared against each")
    RAND
    (PARTY "a" MUST deliver WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `each of the pair, breach first` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 20
